  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The short answer",
      "items": [
        "The router reads the workspace's file list from SQLite, including each file's size and the CRC-32 computed during upload, and hands it to the Zip streamer, which writes zip headers and streams each file's bytes straight from the file store",
        "Nothing is written to disk and no file is read twice"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not shown here",
      "items": [
        "Compression: the zip is store-only, since most shared files (photos, video, PDFs) are already compressed",
        "Connected but out of scope: cloudflared tunnel, Access keys, Chunked uploads, Guest links, Expiry sweeper, Env file"
      ]
    }
  ]
